  Literate programming plays a central role in reproducible science to
  build reports from the computer code of analyses. In the R
  ecosystem, Sweave is widely used to build documentation this way.
  This note sheds some light on the perhaps lesser known, or
  exploited, component of literate programming, at least in scientific
  computing: the \emph{tangle} step. I will describe a use case where
  a clever combination of weaving and tangling allows efficiently
  maintaining elaborate documents built from components of various types.
